hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16715","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from a man of the Ansar from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that qasama was in the jahiliyya, the qasama of blood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) affirmed it upon what it had been upon in the jahiliyya, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by it between people of the Ansar from Banu Haritha who claimed it against the Jews."
"16726","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiya, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr, he said: the Ansari, the keeper of the sacrificial camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent him, he said: I returned and said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me with what perishes of them; he said: Slaughter it, then dye its sandal in its blood, then place it on its side or on its flank, and do not eat from it, you nor anyone of your company."
"16762","He said: Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Zaida narrated to us, he said: al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi ibn Umayla narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from a man of the Ansar, from the Prophet: Horses are three: a horse a man ties in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, so its price is reward and its riding is reward and its lending is reward and its fodder is reward; and a horse upon which a man bets and races, so its price is sin and its fodder is sin; and a horse for the belly, and it may be a sufficiency against poverty, if Allah, exalted, wills."
"23881","Isma'il narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to me from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq from a man of the Ansar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finds a louse in his garment, let him press it and not throw it in the mosque."
"24037","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Ibn Lahiah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah ibn Khudayj, he said: I heard a man of Kindah say: A man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the Ansar narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one of you falls short in his prayer except Allah, Mighty and Majestic, completes it for him from his supererogatory."
"24082","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed to us Ibn Jurayj, informed to me Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from a man of the Ansar, that the Ansari informed Ata that he kissed his wife in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while fasting. So he commanded his wife, and she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Messenger of Allah does that. So his wife informed him, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is allowed things. Go back to him and say to him. So she returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is allowed things. So he said: I am the most God-fearing of you to Allah, and the most knowing of you of the bounds of Allah."
